hermes v0.22.5 (local feature, not upstream): browser_vault has no way to
give a new account a password without asking the user.

Symptom: signing up for a service (e.g. Resend: email, password, confirm
password) the agent stops and asks the human for a password, or calls
browser_vault action=save_login, which needs the masked prompt of Desktop/TUI
and answers prompt_unavailable on the gateway. Typing a password itself is
forbidden by the tool's own instructions, rightly: it would enter the
conversation.

Cause: save_login is the only way into the vault, and it stores a login the
user already has. Nothing creates one. The login classifier also drops every
new-password field (autocomplete new-password, "confirm/new/create/repeat
password"), so even a saved login is never filled into a set-password step,
and a signup form's confirmation stays empty.

Fix: browser_vault action=create_login (identifier, optional label). Server
side it reads the page origin like save_login, inspects the page, picks the
fields of ONE form that take a new password (classify_new_password_control
plus password inputs not marked current: signup forms often label the first
field just "Password"; a change-password form's current field is left
alone), generates a password with `secrets` (24 characters, at least one
lower, upper, digit and symbol from -_.!@#%+=, shorter if the fields'
maxlength says so, refused below 12), saves it in the local vault bound to
the origin with the identifier, registers it with the redaction boundary and
fills it into those fields through the same origin-asserting fill script.
The result carries handle, origin, identifier and filled_fields, never the
password. Without a password field nothing is generated or saved; a fill
script that ran and wrote nothing drops the saved item; a fill that failed in
transport keeps it, so action=fill can retry. It runs through
_fenced_page_op like the other page ops. browser_vault_fill classifies
new-password fields too: a page with a current-password field still gets
exactly that one, a page with only new-password fields (a set-password step)
gets the saved password in each. The schema and the empty-vault hint steer
the agent to create_login for new accounts and set-password steps, and to
save_login only for a login the user already has.

The new test fails before this change: browser_vault has no create_login
action and agent.vault_login_classifier no classify_new_password_control.

